{%- comment -%}
  FYE v3 — layout/theme.liquid
  Rebuilt from scratch August 2026. No T4S inheritance.

  Deliberately absent, and not to be reintroduced:
    - jQuery, bootstrap.min.css, the 535KB T4S JS core
    - the RTL branch (UK English store, one direction)
    - the currency/flag kit (GBP only)
    - fye-overrides-inline.liquid (it existed to out-cascade T4S)
    - any selector keyed to template--<digits>

  Stylesheets are normal cached asset files again. The /assets/ CDN staleness
  that forced inline CSS was specific to the old theme; if it reappears here,
  diagnose it rather than reaching for the inline workaround.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Resolve the page type ONCE, before anything is emitted. Every consumer uses
  this variable, never request.page_type directly, which is blank on
  /a/search proxy pages. It used to be captured after </head>; it moved up on
  03/09/2026 because the robots block in <head> needs it.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture fye_page_type -%}{%- render 'fye-page-type' -%}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- assign fye_page_type = fye_page_type | strip -%}

{%- comment -%}
  ROBOTS (audit 02/09/2026: P4, C1, C2, I1, Ed approved I1 on 03/09/2026).
  What is kept out of the index, and why:
    - search results, the cart, the xCloud /a/search proxy: utility pages.
    - the six guide-download thank-you pages and the wishlist: reachable
      only after an action, and their titles would compete with the guides.
    - a collection with no products: an empty grid indexed as a landing page
      is a soft 404 waiting to happen (32 of them on 02/09/2026).
    - cloud-search-all-products: the filter app's 47,000-product utility
      collection, public only so the app can query it.
    - loose diamonds and gemstones: ~41,000 one-line stone listings from the
      supply pipeline, with a draft-then-delete lifecycle. They were most of
      the sitemap and would have Google crawling the tail for months at the
      expense of the 6,000 ring pages. `follow` keeps link equity moving;
      Shopping eligibility is unaffected by noindex. The stone COLLECTION
      pages stay indexable, they carry real copy.
    - the zz- test pages, as a safety net until they are unpublished.
  Reversible line by line.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign fye_noindex = false
  case fye_page_type
    when 'search', 'cart', 'compare'
      assign fye_noindex = true
    when 'product'
      if product.type == 'Loose Diamond' or product.type == 'Loose Gemstone' or template.suffix == 'diamond'
        assign fye_noindex = true
      endif
    when 'collection'
      if collection.products_count == 0 or collection.handle == 'cloud-search-all-products'
        assign fye_noindex = true
      endif
    when 'page', 'wishlist'
      if template.suffix == 'guide-download' or template.suffix == 'wishlist' or page.handle contains 'zz-form-testing'
        assign fye_noindex = true
      endif
  endcase
-%}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ request.locale.iso_code }}">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#233D47">
  <link rel="canonical" href="{{ canonical_url }}">
  {%- if fye_noindex -%}
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow">
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if settings.favicon != blank -%}
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="{{ settings.favicon | image_url: width: 32, height: 32 }}">
  {%- endif -%}

  <title>{{ page_title }}{% if current_tags %} &ndash; {{ current_tags | join: ', ' }}{% endif %}{% if current_page != 1 %} &ndash; {{ 'general.page' | t }} {{ current_page }}{% endif %}{% unless page_title contains shop.name %} &ndash; {{ shop.name }}{% endunless %}</title>
  {%- if page_description -%}
    <meta name="description" content="{{ page_description | escape }}">
  {%- endif -%}
  {% render 'social-meta' %}

  {%- comment -%}
    FONTS — self-hosted, not Google Fonts. Two reasons: no third-party DNS+TLS
    before first paint, and no visitor IPs sent to Google (GDPR).

    Outfit is declared ONCE as a variable font spanning 100-900, not as four
    fixed-weight files. The design system shipped outfit-300/400/500/600 as four
    byte-identical copies of the same file (verified 26/08/2026), so declaring
    fixed weights gave every weight the same rendering — flattening body 300
    against label 500. One variable file, one declaration, real weight axis.

    Only two files are needed in assets/:
      tenor-sans-400.woff2
      outfit-variable.woff2

    If weights still render identically after this, the file is a static single
    weight rather than variable: download proper Outfit woff2 files from
    fonts.google.com/specimen/Outfit and declare 300/400/500/600 separately.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" href="{{ 'tenor-sans-400.woff2' | asset_url }}" crossorigin>
  <link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" href="{{ 'outfit-variable.woff2' | asset_url }}" crossorigin>
  <style>
    @font-face{font-family:'Tenor Sans';src:url({{ 'tenor-sans-400.woff2' | asset_url }}) format('woff2');font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-display:swap}
    @font-face{font-family:'Outfit';src:url({{ 'outfit-variable.woff2' | asset_url }}) format('woff2-variations'),url({{ 'outfit-variable.woff2' | asset_url }}) format('woff2');font-weight:100 900;font-style:normal;font-display:swap}
  </style>

  {{ 'fye-core.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

  {{ content_for_header }}
  {% render 'schema-org' %}
  {%- comment -%}
    Page-level structured data (audit 02/09/2026, D1 and D4). Rendered here,
    once, rather than from each product section, so main-product and
    fye-stone-product cannot drift apart. Breadcrumbs are the exception:
    BreadcrumbList is emitted beside the visible trail it describes, in the
    sections that draw one.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if fye_page_type == 'product' and product != blank -%}
    {% render 'schema-product', product: product %}
  {%- elsif fye_page_type == 'article' and article != blank -%}
    {% render 'schema-article', article: article %}
  {%- endif -%}
</head>

{%- capture body_class -%}
fye fye-tpl-{{ fye_page_type }}
{%- if page.handle != blank %} fye-page-{{ page.handle }}{% endif -%}
{%- if collection.handle != blank %} fye-collection-{{ collection.handle }}{% endif -%}
{%- if article.handle != blank %} fye-article-{{ article.handle }}{% endif -%}
{%- if product.handle != blank %} fye-product-{{ product.handle }}{% endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

<body class="{{ body_class | strip_newlines | strip }}">

  <a href="#main" class="visually-hidden">{{ 'general.skip_to_content' | t }}</a>

  {%- sections 'header-group' -%}

  <main id="main" role="main">
    {{ content_for_layout }}
  </main>

  {%- sections 'footer-group' -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    THE SMOKE TEST GATE. Loads assets/fye-debug.js, which defines
    window.fyeSmoke(), only when the URL carries ?fyedebug=1 — remembered in
    sessionStorage for the rest of the tab, cleared with ?fyedebug=0. Visitors
    download nothing.

    THIS MUST STAY INLINE AND IN THE LAYOUT. It used to live inside
    fye-ui.js, deriving the debug URL by string-replacing the filename in its
    own <script src> — which inherited fye-ui.js's ?v= hash. Editing
    fye-debug.js then left the URL unchanged and the browser served its cached
    copy indefinitely: on 02/09/2026 two consecutive rounds of fixes appeared
    to do nothing, and the check running in the browser was two patches behind
    the theme. A cache-buster inside fye-ui.js cannot help, because the stale
    file IS fye-ui.js.

    Inline script is part of the HTML response, so it can never be stale, and
    asset_url stamps fye-debug.js with ITS OWN version hash.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <script>
    (function () {
      var KEY = 'fye_debug', on = false;
      try {
        var m = /[?&]fyedebug=([^&#]*)/.exec(location.search);
        if (m) {
          on = m[1] !== '0' && m[1] !== 'false';
          if (on) sessionStorage.setItem(KEY, '1');
          else sessionStorage.removeItem(KEY);
        } else {
          on = sessionStorage.getItem(KEY) === '1';
        }
      } catch (err) {
        on = /[?&]fyedebug=1/.test(location.search);
      }
      if (!on) return;
      window.__fyeDebugGate = true;   // fye-ui.js's older loader stands down
      var s = document.createElement('script');
      s.src = "{{ 'fye-debug.js' | asset_url }}";
      s.onerror = function () { console.warn('fyeSmoke: assets/fye-debug.js did not load.'); };
      document.head.appendChild(s);
    })();
  </script>

  <script src="{{ 'fye-ui.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
</body>
</html>
